# config.py and the worker both load .env.txt, so it holds real keys — the
# database URL, the publishing tokens, JWT_SECRET. It was NOT covered by the
# patterns above, which meant a plain `git add -A` staged it. Nothing has ever
# committed it; this is what keeps that true.
.env.txt

